11180	{"artifactId":"LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-20T08:33:03.017Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed compatibility behavior satisfies the currently approved upstream acceptance criteria and constraints.","evidence":"The approved DEF still says ac1 requires 'every existing artifact keeps its id and file name, and no stored reference stops resolving'; k2 says 'An artifact id never changes once created'. Rejecting uppercase artifacts contradicts these requirements. The LLD acknowledges this, but its proposed prerequisite has not yet changed the stored DEF. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json]","action":"Complete the stated upstream amendment and approval prerequisite before treating this design as implementable.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current anchor resolution falls back to an artifact's own creation time, including an unstamped standalone LLD.","evidence":"workItemAnchorCreatedAt returns 'meta.epicCreatedAt ?? meta.createdAt'. readEpicDefinitionCore uses 'readEpicCreatedAtStamp(repoPath, lldId) ?? lld.createdAt'. buildRecordFolderArgs also falls through upstream.createdAt, head.createdAt and ownCreatedAt. finalizeStandaloneLld omits epicCreatedAt when no head supplies it. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"Retain the head-kind and first-root stamping changes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Validation writes TESTS before invoking the judge, and both validation and completion compute workflow-owned paths before persisting BUILD.","evidence":"runValidateSession calls persistTestRecordTask before provider.runReviewSession, then calls storyWorkflowFiles before persistBuildRecord. ensureBuildRecordOnCompletion has the same path-before-persist order. storyWorkflowFiles calls buildRecordPathsFor immediately and catches errors only around testRecordPaths. [files: src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/validate.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/own-files.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts]","action":"Retain explicit write intent at both pre-persist callers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Exact artifact-title lookup is a new TrackerPort capability; strict label lookup and adapter error handling already exist.","evidence":"TrackerPort declares findIssue(labels) and findIssues(labels), but no title lookup. github-adapter.ts delegates these through attempt to ghFindIssueByLabelsStrict and ghListIssuesByLabelsStrict. The strict helpers propagate command failures, and the plural helper explicitly paginates. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Reuse the strict failure mapping and ensure the new title lookup returns complete results across pages, including closed issues.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The change inventory covers the code needed to stop deriving work-item identity from folder names.","evidence":"The omitted refFromDocPath function parses docs paths using '/docs/(?:epics|standalone)/', extracts the folder slug and S-number, and returns a WorkItemRef with 'storyId: `s${Number(storySeg.slice(1))}`'. infer-daemon.ts actively calls it as 'refFromDocPath(h.file)' for semantic parent candidates. Deleting id.ts and changing path-scheme.ts leaves this folder-derived identity route intact. [files: src/workflow/locate/infer.ts, src/workflow/locate/infer-daemon.ts]","action":"Add the locator and semantic-hit mapping to the inventory. Resolve ownership through artifact identity or stored metadata instead of reconstructing it from folder names, and add a regression test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The revised resolveWorkflowRef contract preserves its downstream parent-linking consumers after the hierarchical scheme is removed.","evidence":"ResolvedRef currently includes workflowId and slug, populated with toCanonical(wfid) and toSlug(wfid). locate-parent.ts copies r.slug into WorkItemRef; bugfix/tracker.ts subsequently feeds parentRef.slug to issueForWorkflowId and falls back to an unscoped storyId. The LLD specifies accepted inputs but does not specify replacement values for these output fields or conversion of stored parentRef.slug values. [files: src/workflow/tracker/resolve.ts, src/workflow/locate/locate-parent.ts, src/workflow/bugfix/tracker.ts, src/workflow/types.ts]","action":"Define the new ResolvedRef output semantics and parent-reference conversion explicitly. Test locating and linking a parent in a repository containing multiple epics.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The repository contains 444 uppercase-story artifact files affected by strict lowercase identity.","evidence":"Enumerating .insrc/artifacts/*.json found exactly 444 filenames containing an uppercase -S<number> segment. Current storage ID functions interpolate storyId unchanged, while storyIdToOrdinal accepts both cases. [files: .insrc/artifacts, src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/id.ts]","action":"Retain this conversion inventory and verify rewritten references as well as filenames during s9.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed requirement parser preserves the existing stored grammar and successful result shape.","evidence":"parseFrId matches canonical and dash-separated forms and returns { date, hash8, story: Number(storyStr), fr } or { date, hash8, fr }. fr-id.test.ts asserts { date: '20260717', hash8: '185807ba', story: 2, fr: 5 }. Invalid inputs currently return null, exactly the intentional API change identified by the LLD. [files: src/workflow/id.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/fr-id.test.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/functional-definition.ts]","action":"Keep the stored grammar unchanged while updating callers and invalid-input tests to undefined.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Approving AMD-1 alone establishes an unambiguous replacement RequirementIds.parse signature for downstream stories.","evidence":"The HLD declares parse returning { epicHash, ordinal, storyId? }. AMD-1 is a nonbreaking 'sharedContract.fieldAdd' named 'RequirementIds.parse result'. applyFieldAdd performs 'interfaceSketch: sc.interfaceSketch + marker'; it does not replace the original method signature. Approval would therefore leave the old declaration alongside an added comment describing an incompatible result. [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-1.json, src/workflow/amendments/applier.ts]","action":"Correct the amendment so the effective contract explicitly supersedes the old return type, and classify the signature change accurately before downstream consumption.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The s1 ownership exception for the additional TrackerPort method has been agreed upstream.","evidence":"The HLD assigns tracker port additions to s6. All four inspected pending amendments concern RequirementIds.parse; none records findIssuesByTitleToken ownership. The LLD itself lists the exception as awaiting the user's decision. [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-1.json, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-2.json, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-3.json, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-4.json]","action":"Record the ownership exception in the upstream contract before implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design distinguishes missing-anchor failures from ordinary ledger failures and addresses the actual validation failure boundaries.","evidence":"Validation currently catches TESTS persistence errors, separately catches path errors inside testRecordMd, and catches BUILD persistence errors. The proposed contract explicitly surfaces read-intent MissingAnchorError while preserving ordinary best-effort failures. Holding one write root also covers the actual path where TESTS persistence fails before BUILD path calculation. [files: src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/validate.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/test-record.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts]","action":"Ensure implementation changes the inner testRecordMd catch as well as both persistence catches, and converts rethrown MissingAnchorError into the promised BuildStepError.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed ac2 and ac3 tests exercise the relevant real integration boundaries using available seams.","evidence":"validate.ts provides provider, check-runner, clock and TESTS-writer overrides matching the proposed failure scenarios. Completion accepts a listChanged seam. The tracker has a gh execution seam, and the design explicitly adds the missing legacy tracker injection. These support testing cross-day retries, TESTS failure with successful judging, completion-first writes and guarded tracker creation. [files: src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/validate.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts]","action":"Retain these integration tests. Add coverage for locator identity and parent-linking consumers identified above; the ac1 tests remain conditional on the upstream requirement change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":2,"low":9,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-20T08:33:03.017Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
